From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nougat: true multipoint A2DP sink (一拖二) - dual SCB slots,
 active-stream routing, per-peer codec switch

Two peers can now stay connected simultaneously; whichever one plays gets
decoded to the shared AudioTrack, the other stands by.

bta: second BTA_AvRegister allocates scb[1] (SEIDs 4-6, own LCB).  New
bta_av_cb.p_active_scb tracks the streaming sink SCB (set in start_ok,
re-scanned in str_stopped/cleanup/suspend/do_close/open_at_inc);
bta_av_stream_data_cback drops media packets of inactive sink streams.
NULL active keeps legacy single-device behaviour.

btif_av: per-slot contexts (btif_av_cb_storage[2]) selected by an event
router (REGISTER sequential, hndl for stream events, bd_addr for
open/pend/config, rc_handle for meta/RC).  Slot 1 is native-only: its
RC/AVRCP events and Java connection/audio-state reports are dropped.
Per-slot codec cfg store; media ownership (audio_active_slot) switches
on START/SUSPEND/CLOSE with clear_track+reset_decoder (no track leak).
Media pump audio-focus gate disabled (framework only tracks slot 0).

btif_avrcp_audio_track: AUDIO_OUTPUT_FLAG_FAST -> NONE (44.1 kHz AAC
from Windows sources was silent on the MTK fast path) + error logs.
---
diff --git a/bta/av/bta_av_aact.c b/bta/av/bta_av_aact.c
index 6c5d874..2c21af6 100644
--- a/bta/av/bta_av_aact.c
+++ b/bta/av/bta_av_aact.c
@@ -575,6 +575,54 @@ static void bta_av_proc_stream_evt(UINT8 handle, BD_ADDR bd_addr, UINT8 event, t
 ** Returns          void
 **
 *******************************************************************************/
+/*******************************************************************************
+**
+** Function         bta_av_update_active_sink_scb
+**
+** Description      Multipoint (一拖二): maintain bta_av_cb.p_active_scb, the
+**                  sink scb whose media packets are currently forwarded to
+**                  the media task.  Called with the scb that is being
+**                  activated (start_ok), or with an scb that is stopping
+**                  (any other caller) in which case we fall back to another
+**                  started sink scb, or NULL when none is left.
+**
+** Returns          void
+**
+*******************************************************************************/
+void bta_av_update_active_sink_scb (tBTA_AV_SCB *p_scb_stop)
+{
+    tBTA_AV_SCB *p_scbi;
+    int i;
+
+    if (p_scb_stop == NULL)
+    {
+        /* activation is handled inline in bta_av_start_ok */
+        return;
+    }
+
+    if (bta_av_cb.p_active_scb != p_scb_stop)
+    {
+        /* the stopping scb is not the active one: nothing to do */
+        return;
+    }
+
+    /* active scb is stopping: fall back to any other started sink scb */
+    bta_av_cb.p_active_scb = NULL;
+    for (i = 0; i < BTA_AV_NUM_STRS; i++)
+    {
+        p_scbi = bta_av_cb.p_scb[i];
+        if (p_scbi && (p_scbi != p_scb_stop) && (p_scbi->chnl == BTA_AV_CHNL_AUDIO) &&
+            p_scbi->started && (p_scbi->seps[p_scbi->sep_idx].tsep == AVDT_TSEP_SNK))
+        {
+            bta_av_cb.p_active_scb = p_scbi;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    APPL_TRACE_EVENT("bta_av_update_active_sink_scb: stop hdl %d, active -> %d",
+                     p_scb_stop->hndl,
+                     bta_av_cb.p_active_scb ? bta_av_cb.p_active_scb->hndl : 0);
+}
+
 void bta_av_stream_data_cback(UINT8 handle, BT_HDR *p_pkt, UINT32 time_stamp, UINT8 m_pt)
 {
     int index = 0;
@@ -594,6 +642,15 @@ void bta_av_stream_data_cback(UINT8 handle, BT_HDR *p_pkt, UINT32 time_stamp, UI
         osi_free(p_pkt);
         return;
     }
+    /* Multipoint: when one sink stream is active, drop media packets that
